SUMMARY:Myths and Minibeasts: Pollinators
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators have been an important part of human cultural history from the earliest recorded stories and histories.  From “telling the bees” your important family milestones to keep honey flowing to beliefs that souls were carried into the afterlife by butterflies\, pollinators have been featured heavily in myths and stories for millennia.  We’ll dive into some of this folklore\, and talk about some of the common species right outside your door in this virtual program for ages 12+. \nRegister
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/myths-and-minibeasts-pollinators/
LOCATION:Virtual\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Citizen Science,Teens,Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="Jennifer%20Tredway":MAILTO:jennifer.tredway@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
