UID:114806-1781285400-1781301600@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Museum Movie Night: The Goonies
DESCRIPTION:Sold Out!\nDon’t miss the next Museum Movie Night! Check out the upcoming movies and learn more about Museum Movie Night: Where Science meets the Cinema. \n\nThe Goonies (1985)\n“Goonies never say die!” \nAdventure calls\, and it’s hiding in a pirate’s treasure map! Follow a gang of misfit kids through booby-trapped tunnels\, secret caves\, and wild inventions as they hunt for One-Eyed Willy’s gold. Friendship\, danger\, and plenty of “Hey you guys!” await. \nThis movie is rated PG. \nMuseum Movie Night is a night of movies\, music\, and mind-blowing fun. Before the show\, enjoy live tunes\, hands-on science activities\, and tasty food and drinks. After the credits roll\, stick around for a science chat with an expert and movie trivia\, all hosted by A/V Geeks! \n  \n  \n\nSchedule\n5:30pm–7pm: Live music and science stations. Food and drinks for sale.\n7pm: Movie begins in the WRAL 3D Theater\, followed by commentary and movie trivia. \nExhibits and Activities (5:30pm-7pm)\nPirate Bread Tags\nMake a mini One-Eyed-Willie magnet out of a bread tag! \nRope Making\nDon’t venture into the caves without a hearty supply of ropes! Learn to make your own with natural fibers from Museum educator Bob Alderink. \nAlchemy\nTurn pennies into “rich stuff” via amazing alchemy! \nSkeletons\nThe kids come across a lot of skeletons in The Goonies…how good are you at identifying human bones? \nAnimals of the Pacific Northwest\nThe Pacific Northwest is home to some special animals like otters\, spotted owls and banana slugs. Come learn about these cool critters so you are ready the next time you visit Astoria! \nTreasure Hunt\nHow good are you at reading treasure maps? See you if can locate the treasure around the first floor of the Museum! \n\nExpert\n \nDr. Abby Gancz is an archaeologist who uses human skeletal remains and molecular evidence to reconstruct the lives\, health\, and deaths of people from the past. She has worked with ancient human remains from around the world and is interested in how human-associated microbes have evolved alongside us and continue to shape our health today. Following the screening of The Goonies\, she looks forward to sharing what it is like to excavate and study ancient skeletons\, as well as the hidden treasures and stories waiting to be uncovered within our bones. \n\nMUSIC (5:30–7PM)\n\nSinger/songwriter William Woltz is a North Carolina native who covers a lot of musical territory. He grew up loving both the Beatles and Buck Owens while studying jazz and classical guitar. These days he plays a mix of bluesy originals and interesting cover tunes\, always striving for the right blend of old favorites and unexpected treasures. Come prepared to be entertained.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/museum-movie-night-goonies/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Children,General Events,Museum Movie Night,Special Events,Teens,WRAL 3D Theater
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/The_Goonies.jpg
